      "review_date": "2020-03-04 00:28:14",
      "review_stars": 4.0,
      "review_text": "Came here on a Sunday evening with the family! I had a smoothie and my family ordered ice cream. Everything tasted great, and the servers were super kind and friendly. Unfortunately, the store was super crowded when we came, and they were definitely understaffed with only two people working, but the workers were so sweet and handled it well."
    },
    {
      "review_date": "2020-03-03 23:58:01",
      "review_stars": 4.0,
      "review_text": "Love that they are open late for that late night sugar fix! Their brown butter chocolate chip cookies are addictive, make sure you ask them to warm it up so they're ooey gooey. I knocked a star off for the very watery and extremely sweet a\u00e7a\u00ed bowl I got, but I also didn't have high standards for a sweets shop to make a proper a\u00e7a\u00ed bowl."
    },
    {
      "review_date": "2020-01-13 18:04:20",
      "review_stars": 2.0,
      "review_text": "Dear IV Drip, \nI'm sorry, but Yelp's phrase for two stars, \"meh, I've experienced better\" was pretty much my experience with you. There are a fair number of high-star reviews here, and I don't generally like to post low-star reviews. But let me outline the reasons why I am:\n\n- Despite the shop's own employees acknowledging that they should have vegan options in their sweet baked goods and/or ice cream, they don't. There are a lot of vegans in this area and it just makes sense to offer vegan options, both for environmental and capitalist reasons (you'd sell many vegan cookies, I promise)\n- While one server was friendly, the other staff member seemed absolutely bored and lackadaisical (adjective: lacking enthusiasm and determination; carelessly)\n- My Americano tasted much more watery than an Americano is meant to (it's my drink of choice and while my experience does not account for a thorough sampling of all Americanos in existence, I do feel qualified to make this judgment)\n- The cup it was served in had a few spots where a dried unknown substance clung to its outer lip (but hey, at least you do ceramic reusable mugs)\n- Despite shaking the jug of oatmilk on the counter which I decided to add to my Americano to try and improve the drink, what came out was a watered-down stream of almost clear liquid. As I mentioned, I shook the jug, so this wasn't just due to the natural sedimentation of plant milks\n- I had contacted your shop via Facebook before I ever visited to ask about catering an event, and never received a reply--even though this is at present their only mode of contact aside from walking in\n\nSadly, this earns two stars. IV Drip, you can do better."
    }
  ],
